  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Heidenhain DIN/ISO post (`assets/posts/heidenhain.cps`) now writes PECK and DEEP holes as the expanded chain in plain `G00` / `G01` blocks. This occurs at each R clearance. The post writes no `G205` and no peck `G200`.\n\n- The old `G205` had `Q257` = `Q202` = the peck and `Q258=0`. The control made a full retract after each infeed, then moved at FMAX to the cut face.\n- The old peck `G200` had `Q200=0`. The control moved at FMAX to the last depth.\n- The chain makes chip-break hops (PECK), or rapids to R and feeds down from R (DEEP). The simulation and the gouge check read the chain. The posted blocks are now that chain, move for move.\n- DRILL and SPOT keep `G200`, with `Q202` = the whole depth (one infeed). Taps keep `G206` / `G207`.\n- The `Q208` retract-feed code was only for `G205`, so this PR removes it. The `Q395` level guard of `G200` stays. A test pins its refusal.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/4224-heidenhain-peck-chain.md`. It gives what was chosen, why, and what was dropped. A corrected native `G205` was dropped: the cited manuals do not prove its motion equal to the chain.\n\n## Readings\n\nGolden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/heidenhain/drill_peck.nc`, block N100 and after:\n\n```\nN100 G01 X+20 Y+10 Z-18 F60*\nN110 G00 X+20 Y+10 Z-17*\nN120 G01 X+20 Y+10 Z-24 F60*\nN130 G00 X+20 Y+10 Z+0*\n```\n\nThe 1 mm chip-break hop (Z-18 to Z-17) and the feed from the hop agree with `crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `heidenhain_cycles::peck_and_deep_post_the_checked_chain_not_a_native_cycle`: the exact PECK and DEEP blocks, with no `G205`, `G200`, `Q258` or `M99`.\n- `heidenhain_cycles::levels::*`: the peck chain on each control level; `G200` without `Q395` before the Q395 level and with it after.\n- `heidenhain_cycles::levels::a_q395_ask_the_340_49x_cycle_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name`: this replaces the `Q208` refusal test of `G205`.\n- `heidenhain_block_form::heidenhain_native_cycles_and_preset_use_numbered_tnc_blocks`: `G205` is not in the G-word allow-list, and the peck chain blocks are present.\n- `conformance::every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact`: with the updated golden.\n\n## Gate (head 8bdabe9bc)\n\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 791 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Example catalog suites: `example_catalog` 44 passed (4 ignored); `example_catalog_adaptive` 1 passed; `example_catalog_edge_work` 1 passed.\n- `camcraft-post --test cycle_hop`: 7 passed.\n- Light lane `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Targeted heavy step (P1 rule): not applicable. No `#[ignore]`d test in any test file names the Heidenhain post or its goldens. `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` reaches the app heavy lanes only because `heidenhain.cps` contains the word \"heidenhain\". No heavy binary holds a test of the changed code, so no step was run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a control. The posted program is longer, but each block is a plain move that the post already wrote for peck holes with R above the surface.\n\nChangelog: Heidenhain DIN/ISO: PECK and DEEP holes post the checked chain as plain moves. The post writes no `G205` and no peck `G200`, which moved at FMAX to the cut face.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4224\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
